    {
      "v": 2,
      "zh": "那时，耶和华晓谕亚摩斯的儿子以赛亚说：「你去解掉你腰间的麻布，脱下你脚上的鞋。」以赛亚就这样做，露身赤脚行走。",
      "en": "At that time the Lord announced through[NOTE:1] Isaiah son of Amoz: “Go, remove the sackcloth from your waist and take your sandals off your feet.” He did as instructed and walked around in undergarments[NOTE:2] and barefoot.",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “spoke by the hand of.”",
        "The word used here (עָרוֹם, ʿarom) sometimes means “naked,” but here it appears to mean simply “lightly dressed,” i.e., stripped to one’s undergarments. See HALOT 883 s.v. עָרוֹם. The term also occurs in vv. 3, 4."
      ],
